Imports:
  - Types:
      - LazyLoader
    From: salt/loader

Annotations: |
  This cell is salt/returners — 11 job-result storage backends, collected into a `LazyLoader`
  (tag "returner", packed as __salt__) by salt.loader.returners and invoked automatically
  whenever a minion or master needs to persist a job's return data or read it back. Every
  returner backend implements the same conventional function names regardless of storage medium
  (local files, SQL, syslog, ...); this CODEMANIFEST documents that convention through
  local_cache.py, Salt's built-in default (on-disk, under <cachedir>/jobs/) implementation of
  it, which also doubles as the master's job cache even when a different returner is configured
  for external reporting.

---

"returner(load: dict[str, object])":
  location: local_cache.py
  annotations: |
    Persist one job's return data, called once per minion return.

    `load`: the return payload, including at minimum the job id, minion id, and the function's
    result

"prep_jid(nocache: bool, passed_jid: str | None, recurse_count: int) -> jid:str":
  location: local_cache.py
  annotations: |
    Allocate (or reuse, if `passed_jid` is given) a job id and its on-disk job directory before a
    job is published.

    `nocache`: when true, mark the job as one whose returns should not be cached
    `passed_jid`: reuse this job id instead of generating a new one

"save_load(jid: str, clear_load: dict[str, object], minions: list[str] | None, recurse_count: int)":
  location: local_cache.py
  annotations: |
    Persist the publish-time job load (the command and its targeting) alongside the job id, so it
    can be looked up later independent of any single minion's return.

"get_jid(jid: str) -> job_returns:dict[str, object]":
  location: local_cache.py
  annotations: |
    Return every minion's recorded result for job `jid`.

"get_jids() -> jids:list[str]":
  location: local_cache.py
  annotations: |
    List every job id currently present in the local job cache.

"clean_old_jobs()":
  location: local_cache.py
  annotations: |
    Purge job directories older than the configured retention window from the local job cache.

